{
  "$comment": "The site page region contract. Per page type: the regions in drawing order, the part that fills each and the prop that feeds it (slot), the DOM marks (data-slot) that place an element in it, the named parts inside it a rendered check measures, the control kinds it may hold, the parts whose width the layout decides (widths: \"root\" or a part name; a rendered compare holds those widths to 1px and leaves text-driven ones alone) and whether the region may draw a card (carded: a root or part rounded with --site-radius-xl, which the site-demo selftest plants and must find wherever a page draws it). A type is `ready` when the kit draws every region it lists, or `planned` with the reason it is not yet. scripts/check-site-regions.mjs holds the contract to site-core's declared slots; scripts/site-regions-rendered.mjs reads a painted page against it.",
  "version": 1,
  "frame": {
    "$comment": "The window around every page and the column the page's regions stand in; measured on every page type, never a region of its own.",
